      "problem": "$\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$",
