        "answer_fields"
      ]
    },
    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3136",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3332b534-bd04-5e86-995e-1e6d691d8e1b",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using the Pythagorean Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\sin^4{\\theta}+\\sin^2{\\theta}\\cos^2{\\theta}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor $\\sin^2\\theta$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n\\sin^4{\\theta}+\\sin^2{\\theta}\\cos^2{\\theta} = \\sin^2{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^2{\\theta}+\\cos^2{\\theta})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\cos^2\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta = 1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}) & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin^4{\\theta}+\\sin^2{\\theta}\\cos^2{\\theta} = \\sin^2\\theta.\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
      "missing_source_fields": [
        "difficulty",
        "answer_fields"
      ]
    },
    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3137",
      "knowledge_point_id": "868125f0-22e0-57fc-9620-f3242419a689",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying a Rational Expression Using the Pythagorean Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta}{\\sin\\theta}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta} {\\sin \\theta}\t=\t\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\cdot (\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta)} {\\sin \\theta}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot (1)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta} {\\sin \\theta} = \\cot \\theta.\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
      "missing_source_fields": [
        "difficulty",
        "answer_fields"
      ]
    },
    {
